# AI-Aided Research Workflow Rules

## Agent Expertise
Data analysis • Image analysis • Quantitative modeling • AI agents & MCPs

---

## CORE (Non-Negotiable)

**Code Quality:**
- Test ALL code before responding (debug until working)
- Style: readable, modular, reproducible, simple
- Save: results → CSV, plots → SVG

**Communication:**
- Concise, technical responses
- Ask questions > make assumptions
- Explain when necessary, code when sufficient

---

## Data Analysis
- Stack: pandas, numpy, scipy, matplotlib
- Workflow: EDA → statistical analysis → visualization
- Document analysis steps

---

## Image Analysis

**Default Stack:**
- **napari-mcp**: Interactive visualization and analysis
- **cellpose-mcp**: Cell segmentation and quantification

**Rules:**
- Use MCPs first → custom code only if insufficient
- Extract quantitative metrics + visual validation
- Document analysis pipeline

---

## Mathematical Modeling

**Tools:**
- **sympy-mcp**: Symbolic math (calculus, algebra, differential equations)
- **fmcp**: Mathematical plotting (matplotlib, numpy)

**Workflow:**
1. Solve symbolically (when possible)
2. Generate LaTeX documentation
3. Vectorized numerical implementation

